<section class="ref-group"><h2>Battles <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-cynoscephalae"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-cynoscephalae.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Cynoscephalae</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 197 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Cynoscephalae was fought in 197 BCE in Thessaly between the Roman army of Titus Quinctius Flamininus and the Macedonian army of Philip V.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-magnesia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-magnesia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Magnesia</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 190 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Magnesia was fought in 190 BCE in western Anatolia between the Roman Republic, supported by Pergamene allies, and the Seleucid Empire under Antiochus III.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-myonessus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-myonessus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Myonessus</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 190 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Myonessus was a naval battle fought off the coast of Ionia in 190 BCE, in which a Roman and Rhodian fleet under Lucius Aemilius Regillus defeated the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pydna"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-pydna.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Pydna</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 168 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Pydna was fought on 22 June 168 BCE near Pydna in Macedonia, where a Roman army under Lucius Aemilius Paullus defeated King Perseus of Macedon.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-scarpheia"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Scarpheia</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 146 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Scarpheia was fought in 146 BCE near Scarpheia in eastern Locris, at the start of the Achaean War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mobei"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-mobei.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Mobei</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 119 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Mobei was fought in 119 BCE north of the Gobi Desert between the armies of Han China under Wei Qing and Huo Qubing and the Xiongnu.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-muthul"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Muthul</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 109 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Muthul was fought in 109 BCE near the Muthul River in Numidia between the Roman army of the consul Quintus Caecilius Metellus and King Jugurtha.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-vercellae"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-vercellae.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Vercellae</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 101 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Vercellae was fought in 101 BCE on the Raudine Plain in northern Italy, where Roman armies under Gaius Marius and Quintus Lutatius Catulus destroyed the…</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Sieges <span class="n">1</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-carthage-149-146-bce"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Carthage (149–146 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 146 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Carthage was the main engagement of the Third Punic War, in which Roman forces besieged the city of Carthage.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Wars &amp; campaigns <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/roman-seleucid-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/roman-seleucid-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Roman–Seleucid War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 192–188 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Roman–Seleucid War was fought from 192 to 188 BCE between the Roman Republic, with its allies Pergamon and Rhodes, and the Seleucid king Antiochus III the Great.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/third-macedonian-war"><span class="enc-name">Third Macedonian War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 171–168 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Third Macedonian War was fought from 171 to 168 BCE between Rome and King Perseus of Macedon.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/third-punic-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/third-punic-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Third Punic War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 149–146 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Third Punic War was the last conflict between Rome and Carthage, fought from 149 to 146 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/achaean-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/achaean-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Achaean War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 146 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Achaean War of 146 BCE was the conflict in which Rome crushed the Achaean League and its allies in southern Greece.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/han-xiongnu-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/han-xiongnu-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Han–Xiongnu War</span><span class="enc-type">War · from 129 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Han–Xiongnu War was a long series of conflicts between the Han Dynasty and the Xiongnu confederation, entering its offensive phase from 129 BCE under Emperor Wu.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cimbrian-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cimbrian-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cimbrian War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 113–101 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Cimbrian War was fought from 113 to 101 BCE between the Roman Republic and the migrating Cimbri and Teutones.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/jugurthine-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jugurthine-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Jugurthine War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 112–105 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Jugurthine War was fought from 112 to 105 BCE between the Roman Republic and Jugurtha, king of Numidia.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Revolts &amp; revolutions <span class="n">1</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/maccabean-revolt"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/maccabean-revolt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Maccabean Revolt</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · 167–142 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Maccabean Revolt was a Jewish uprising against the Seleucid Empire lasting from 167 to 142 BCE, provoked by the religious policies of Antiochus IV.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Treaties <span class="n">1</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-apamea"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/treaty-of-apamea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Treaty of Apamea</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · Peace · 188 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Treaty of Apamea was the peace settlement of 188 BCE between Rome and the Seleucid king Antiochus III after his defeat at the Battle of Magnesia.</span></a></li></ul></section>
